direction: down

title: |md
  ### TCP ownership and TSQ: retained originals vs downstream clones
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

writeq: "TCP write queue" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  w_body: |md
    New data skb starts on `sk_write_queue`.

    `sk_wmem_queued` is charged when TCP
    creates/appends the skb.

    tcp_write_xmit checks cwnd, rwnd,
    Nagle, TSO, and pacing constraints.
  |
}

rtxq: "TCP retransmit tree" {
  style.fill: "#ede9fe"
  r_body: |md
    After first successful transmission,
    `tcp_event_new_data_sent()` moves the
    original skb:

    `sk_write_queue` → `tcp_rtx_queue`

    The `sk_wmem_queued` charge remains
    until ACK/free (`tcp_wmem_free_skb`).
  |
}

check: "TSQ gate before another send" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  c_body: |md
    `tcp_small_queue_check()` compares
    `sk_wmem_alloc` with:

    min(max(2 × skb->truesize,
            pacing_rate >> pacing_shift),
        tcp_limit_output_bytes)

    Usually a two-skb floor or ~1 ms of
    pacing-rate bytes per socket.
  |
}

clone: "Downstream transmit clone" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  cl_body: |md
    `tcp_transmit_skb()` normally clones
    the retained TCP skb for output.

    The clone is charged to `sk_wmem_alloc`
    and gets destructor `tcp_wfree`.

    It can occupy IP/qdisc/device queues;
    it is not the retained rtx-tree original.
  |
}

throttle: "Over limit: TSQ_THROTTLED" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  t_body: |md
    Stop sending another skb.

    Not-yet-sent originals stay on the write
    queue; already-sent originals remain in
    the retransmit tree.

    This bounds one socket's occupancy below
    TCP, not aggregate backlog across flows.
  |
}

free: "Downstream release: tcp_wfree" {
  style.fill: "#fff7ed"
  f_body: |md
    Remove the clone's `sk_wmem_alloc` charge.

    If TSQ throttled this socket, queue it on
    per-CPU BH work so tcp_write_xmit can retry
    outside the qdisc-locking context.
  |
}

writeq -> check: "consider next unsent skb"
check -> clone: "under limit: transmit clone"
clone -> rtxq: "successful first send retains original"
check -> throttle: "still over limit" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
clone -> free: "qdisc/device releases clone"
free -> check: "wake and try more" {style.stroke: "#16a34a"}
throttle -> free: "wait for a prior clone to drain" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
